um i think one of the most remarkable  things that uh we found during the asap  program and and again uh the osap  program uh was a 24-month program that  started  in uh 2008 and ended in 2010  but you know for the first time we had a  large team we had about 50 people who  were employed full-time at osap and then  we had 22 million dollars allocated  through the defense intelligence agency  for a two-year period so  it's very rare in the ufo field to have  the luxury of resources and being able  to study people over long periods of  time after you know they've encountered  ufos so i guess one of the most  remarkable sort of  um discoveries that we made uh during  the asap program was  the intense medical effects  that that uh that some of these uh ufo  um  cases  cause in in in some people i'll give you  an example um  one of the one of the sentinel cases  that we actually investigated over  about a year actually and and it went  into almost a two-year investigation  was that this biotechnologist and his  daughter were driving towards bend  oregon in their in their vehicle on  their way home and the daughter notices  three small ufos  uh bluish-colored that were darting  around in the field beside them  once she noticed them they immediately  made a beeline for the vehicle as they  were driving and uh one of them went  right across the windshield one of them  went uh came into the car  and and went right across uh both the in  their field of view went right across  the uh the windshield  inside the vehicle but the third one  actually went through the left shoulder  of this biotechnologist  went through the upper thoracic cavity  and then emerged from the right shoulder  and then shot out through the  the window right in front of the  daughter i mean this was a terrifying  episode for the for the daughter  especially uh she was witnessing all of  this  but you know within um i would say 24 to  48 hours uh this guy woke up the  following day with the let the left side  of his face was all sunburned  um his his ear had started swelling his  eye he was started  losing the sight in his left eye  within a week or  a couple of weeks he started losing his  hair on the left side of his head and  you know luckily we had on contract md  phd  a couple of md phds  um really sort of as as people who could  get deep into medical investigations and  look at medical injuries so we deployed  one of these people uh you know on this  case and he followed he followed this  guy over many many months but um it  turned out that  a few months after this this event had  happened  he came down with a rare form of ductile  carcinoma  that locally was not metastatic so it it  did not metastasize  and over a two year period went through  a lot of a lot of health  issues  but in terms of being able to document  all of that we were very very fortunate  that we had access to blood samples  taken  from this guy before the incident and  then there were multiple blood samples  taken  after the incident  so we were able to  piece together a medical forensic sort  of picture of what had happened  before and uh and after this incident  and we could document you know  rises and falls of various immune immune  system parameters within this guy uh we  we we saw that there were dramatic  changes in neutrophil lymphocyte ratios  over time and you know this was for from  a an awesome  ufo investigation point of view we think  this was one of the sentinel cases  because  we we had resources and we were able to  we had the luxury of following this guy  over a year and a half to two years  after the incident and as i said we had  blood samples taken before the incident  so we were actually able to  postulate about cause and effect and the  sort of the dramatic increase in adverse  health symptoms that this guy had  uh  suffered um we were able to say with  reasonable confidence that he suffered  pretty well all of those after the uh  close encounter with this uh small blue  orb um so that that's that was the case  and we had uh several other cases  that uh bass asap encountered that sort  of um you know looked at the medical  injury aspect and that was one of the  things that really surprised me  during the mis the niz era we did not  encounter too many of those cases um you  know we were all the time database in  cases  from um you know we had about 1 800  separate ufo investigations under our  belt by the time the nids database uh  went on ice which was about 2003  um but we never saw in in terms of boots  in the ground investigations of ufo  effects we never saw the sort of level  of medical injury uh that we saw sort of  you know up close and personal with a  few of these cases so i guess that's one  of the things that really surprised me  from the awesome uh series of  investigations  did that person feel any burning  sensation or any sensation at all when  the orb went through him  well he he actually did feel a sort of  really weird sort of uncomfortable  um it wasn't painful or or  anything he he felt sort of um  discombobulated and sort of out of sorts  as this thing was traveling through his  body it was almost like  a large it felt like a very very large  bubble that was moving through his body  he actually did feel the movement but he  didn't feel any pain or he didn't feel  any discomfort he just felt  uh i would say it was sort of a version  of mild vertigo
 

